  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "bit_read_B",
    "file": "libredwg/src/bits.c",
    "description": "The one-bit reader performs an out-of-bounds read because its `CHK_OVERFLOW` guard uses strict `>` comparisons. When the cursor is exactly at EOF (`dat->byte == dat->size` and `dat->bit == 0`), the guard accepts the position, and `bit_read_B` dereferences `dat->chain[dat->byte]`, reading one byte past the heap allocation. The R13/R2000 header decoder also parses header variables without limiting the Bit_Chain to the declared header-section/header-variable extent, allowing malformed data to exhaust the physical input, but the memory-safety failure is the EOF off-by-one in `bit_read_B`/`CHK_OVERFLOW`.",
    "conditions": "The harness recognizes the input as DWG from its `AC` prefix and passes it to `dwg_decode`. Crafted R13/R2000 section metadata reaches `decode_R13_R2000`, which invokes `dwg_decode_header_variables` on the original, unbounded input Bit_Chain. A truncated or undersized header-variable stream causes sequential field decoding to consume all available bytes; in this PoV the next required field is `DIMSOXD` at `header_variables.spec:436`. Its `FIELD_B` call enters `bit_read_B` with `byte == size` and `bit == 0`, bypasses the faulty overflow check, and reads exactly one byte beyond the input buffer."
  },
